  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-3+1-5-5+2-8) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(-3-(-3))^{2}+(1-(-3))^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}+(2-(-3))^{2}+(-8-(-3))^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[0+16+4+4+25+25] \\\\  & =\\frac{74}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
